# =============================================================================
# PRism — .dockerignore
# =============================================================================
# What it does:
# - Prevents sending unnecessary/host-specific files to the Docker daemon
#   (faster `docker build`, smaller context, no secret leaks).
# - Mirrors .gitignore plus Docker-specific exclusions (see comments).
#
# Gotchas:
# - .env is NEVER copied — container must receive env via `--env-file` or
#   `env_file:` in compose. If you `COPY .env` the secret leaks into layer history.
# - `dist/` is ignored here because the builder stage recompiles from `src/` —
#   stale local `dist/` never pollutes the image.
# - Keep `package.json` + `package-lock.json` (required for `npm ci`).
# =============================================================================

# --- Dependencies & build outputs (rebuilt in image) ---
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnp
.pnp.js
dist
build
out
.next
.turbo
.cache

# --- Secrets & local env (CRITICAL: never bake into image) ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.production
*.pem
*.key

# --- Git & OS artifacts ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
*~

# --- Workspace & reports (ephemeral at runtime — mount as volumes) ---
workspace
workspace/
repos
reports
coverage
.nyc_output
.coverage
*.lcov
lcov.info

# --- Dev & CI artifacts (not needed at runtime) ---
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
.token-optimizer
.adk
coverage
tests
vitest.config.ts
eslint.config.*
.prettierrc*
docker-compose.override.yml
# NOTE: tsconfig.json + src/ are intentionally NOT ignored — required for builder stage `npm run build`

# --- Docs & examples (keep README.md for reference, ignore rest) ---
# README.md is intentionally NOT ignored — copied to /app for debugging
# LICENSE is also kept
*.md
!README.md

# --- Docker itself (avoid recursive copy) ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml
.docker

# --- Misc ---
tmp
temp
